step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple mean combination on the full pool to establish a baseline robust to ranking instability.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error to see if it improves on the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full pool to see if it beats the weighted inverse_error.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test the best individual model (ARIMA) to see if a single strong model beats the weighted combo.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ARIMA"}

Thought: Evaluate a trimmed mean over the full pool to see if removing extremes improves the already strong ARIMA performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a dba combination on the full pool to see if a more sophisticated robust method outperforms ARIMA alone.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the reduced pool1 to see if removing less correlated models improves over best_single ARIMA.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on a larger pool (pool2) using inverse_error to see if adding more correlated models helps or hurts.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean on the reduced pool1 to see if removing less correlated models improves over weighted pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the smaller pool2 using the existing inverse_error weight handle (w2) to see if a tighter pool improves performance.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"w2"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the full pool with inverse_error weights to see if it improves over the best single ARIMA.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the reduced pool1 to see if it outperforms the weighted or mean variants.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a DBA (Deterministic Baseline Aggregator) on the reduced pool1 to see if a more sophisticated robust method can beat the current best ARIMA single model.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a dba combination on the larger pool2 to see if more iterative optimization improves over the mean and weighted baselines.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

